  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Data lifelines: sustaining informed and effective humanitarian responseData lifelines: sustaining informed and effective humanitarian response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the humanitarian caseloads continues to increase due to new and protracted crises, 2025 is marked by unique, unprecedented cuts to humanitarian funding that challenge the continuation of common services as well as the overall capacity to provide lifesaving assistance altogether. People-centred and operational relevant data are at the core of a targeted humanitarian planning cycle. The suspension of these services, and the resulting lack of data on human mobility in crisis contexts, affects the entire humanitarian system in its ability to plan, prioritize and target assistance.Through this project, IOM aims to enhance the availability and use of Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) data on mobility and needs for the humanitarian community and activities will strengthen and expand leadership of critical human mobility data to enable both strategic and operational coordination in humanitarian response. This will equip humanitarian actors, both on the ground and at the global level, with the timely and essential information needed to make swift and coordinated decisions.</narrative>
  </description>
